Original commit body from d555315:

For compiled language projects (C, C++, Go, Rust) that use shell scripts
as integration tests, these tests invoke the compiled binary rather than
calling functions directly. This means call graph analysis shows 0%
coverage even when the project has comprehensive integration tests.

This change:
- Adds _detect_project_binary_names() to find executable names from:
  - meson.build: executable('name', ...)
  - Makefile: TARGET = name (and similar variables)
  - CMakeLists.txt: add_executable(name ...)
  - Cargo.toml: [package] name or [[bin]] name
  - go.mod: module path (last component)
  - configure.ac: AC_INIT([name], ...)
  - Falls back to directory name if compiled language source exists

- Adds _detect_shell_integration_tests() to find shell scripts in test
  directories that invoke the project binary

- Updates the Tests section to show hybrid coverage like:
  "~10% estimated coverage + 5 shell integration scripts"

Also improves README intro extraction to complete sentences that span
paragraph breaks - if the extracted text doesn't end with punctuation,
it will append words from the next non-empty line until a period is
reached.
